# Comparison Report

Noise model: sigma_hat = 2.8345e-02 (white; see diagnosis). Residuals normalized by
sigma_hat*sqrt(n) = 4.2233e-01; 1.0 means residual equals the noise level. No method has
access to x_true; every parameter below is data-selected.

| Method | Parameter (auto-selected) | ||Kx-y||/(sigma*sqrt(n)) | ||x||_2 (||D2 x||_2) | 5-fold CV prediction RMS |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| A Tikhonov (L=I, GCV) | lambda = 4.1052e-04 | 0.959 | 5.5286 (12.9575) | 0.03145 |
| B TSVD (block+3sigma cutoff) | k = 22 | 0.992 | 5.0213 (12.1384) | 0.03207 |
| C CGLS (Morozov tau=1.0) | iterations = 12 | 0.998 | 4.4999 (10.5846) | 0.03231 |
| (reference: noise level) | - | 1.000 | - | 0.02835 |

## Parameter selection and sensitivity (reported, not hidden)
- Tikhonov: GCV minimum lambda = 4.105e-04; L-curve corner lambda = 1.848e-02. The two
  criteria DISAGREE by ~45x on this exponential spectrum. Tie-break by
  5-fold predictive CV: CV-optimal lambda = 3.162e-04, which confirms GCV (CV RMS at GCV
  lambda = 0.03145 vs 0.03476 at the L-curve corner). The
  L-curve corner over-smooths here (its residual ratio
  1.13 also exceeds the discrepancy
  level). GCV lambda is therefore adopted. Documented limitation: the GCV minimum is shallow, so
  lambda is uncertain by roughly a decade; GCV also assumes the white-noise model of the
  diagnosis - under colored noise it would be biased.
- TSVD: selected k = 22 (block screening then |u_i^T y| > 3*sigma_hat within the band).
  Sensitivity: tau = 2/3/4/5 -> k = 22/22/18/13; GCV over k ->
  k = 26; CV over k -> k = 28; bootstrap k* = 33.8 +/-
  41.2 (bootstrap overruns are driven by chance 3-sigma noise coefficients at
  high i - the same effect that inflates the raw last-3sigma index to 111).
- CGLS: iteration 12 first crosses ||Kx-y|| <= tau*sigma_hat*sqrt(n) with tau = 1.0 (chosen
  because tau > 1 would stop at an under-fit residual; the discrepancy level 1.0 is where the
  residual energy equals the estimated noise energy). tau = 1.0/1.1/1.2 ->
  12/7/4 iterations. CV-optimal is 21 iterations, i.e.
  Morozov stops about 9 iterations early (documented sensitivity).
- Seminorm check: Tikhonov with L = D2 at the same lambda changes the solution by
  ||x_D2 - x_I||/||x_I|| = 4.49. Because the singular vectors are Haar-rough, no
  smoothness scale in the standard basis is data-supported, so L = I is kept (see diagnosis).

## Cross-method agreement (mutual confidence without ground truth)
- corr(x_A, x_B) = 0.8237,  ||x_A - x_B||/||x_B|| = 0.630
- corr(x_A, x_C) = 0.8937,  ||x_A - x_C||/||x_C|| = 0.559
- corr(x_B, x_C) = 0.9337,  ||x_B - x_C||/||x_C|| = 0.401
All three recover the same low-index content (first ~25 components), differing only
in how they treat the noise-dominated tail.

## Fit, properties, trustworthiness
- Fit: residuals at ~1.0 x noise level for all three; none materially under- or over-fits.
- Properties: ||x||_C <= ||x||_B <= ||x||_A; Tikhonov's smooth filter keeps the borderline
  3-5 sigma components (i ~ 15-25) at partial weight instead of TSVD's accept/reject; CGLS early
  stopping damps them almost entirely.
- Trust: dpc_judgment = does_not_hold and effective_rank = 25 imply only the first
  ~25 coefficients are recoverable; agreement among three independent regularizers
  on that band is the main confidence evidence available without ground truth.

## Recommendation
Recommended: **method_a (Tikhonov, L = I), lambda = 4.1052e-04**.
Justification: (i) residual ratio 0.96 sits at the noise floor implied by
noise_estimate = 2.835e-02 (Morozov-consistent); (ii) GCV selection is corroborated by
independent 5-fold CV (0.03145 vs noise 0.02835) and gives the best CV risk
among the three selected solutions; (iii) the filter band matches effective_rank =
25, beyond which dpc_judgment: does_not_hold forbids keeping coefficients; (iv)
smooth filtering hedges the borderline 3-5 sigma components (i ~ 15-25) that TSVD keeps in full
and CGLS suppresses almost entirely - the honest position given the Picard analysis.
Limitations: the GCV/L-curve disagreement (45x) is resolved by CV, not by a
provably optimal rule; CGLS stopping is strongly tau-dependent; cross-method agreement certifies
the first ~25 components only, not the discarded tail.
recommended_solution.csv is a byte-identical copy of method_a/x_reg.csv.
